    <item>
      <title>From: M., To: Ruby Chandler</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/1910/08/01/1340/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Aug 1910 22:14:25 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/1910/08/01/1340/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140613_16153034_0588&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/postcard-2014-20140613_16153034_0588.jpg&#34;&gt; &lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140613_16154079_0589&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/postcard-2014-20140613_16154079_0589.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;
From: M. To: Ruby Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Mailed From: Pearl, Illinois on August 1, 1910&lt;br&gt;
Postcard Info: Made in Germany&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Miss Ruby D. Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Wichita, Kansas&lt;br&gt;
903 Estelle Ave.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dear Ruby,&lt;br&gt;
We’re quite well my man and I. Clara and Maud came home Saturday. The whole bunch of girls were here yesterday after noon. I missed you. When are you coming home? Big ball game yesterday. Chicago beat Detroit 2 to 0. S.S. Convention also all day yesterday. My space is about taken huh. Had to send you birthday greetings.&lt;br&gt;
Love to All,&lt;br&gt;
Auntie M.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
